speaker.md
## Structure
It is a known layered polar hexagonal antiferromagnet. It has two optically and magnetically active Fe2+ ions, which also show the magnetoelectric effect: you can induce macroscopic polarization by magnetic field and vice versa.

The absence of PT element in the symmetry satisfies the condition for altermagnetism. As you can see by the inset plot, even with high fields the induced magnetization remains zero.

