speaker.md
## Why bother?
The nature and optical properties of low-frequency excitations are quite puzzling. Raman study shows chiral phonons, Neutron scattering shows magnon-polarons: a hybrid of magnon and acoustic phonon away from the Gamma point.

Of course it would be nice to catch the signature band splitting or hybridization at the Gamma point, where we can probe it with our basic optical tools. And see if we can use magnetic-point group analysis, which may not be applicable in the case of ideal altermagnets. This one is not ideal, of course.

