speaker.md
## Our tool
Let's talk about how we probe it. Our tool is time-resolved spectroscopy.
We have a femtosecond laser that generates pulses. When they hit our antenna, the latter generates THz radiation that goes through our sample and then it is captured by a detector. Since it is time-resolved, we see both: phase and amplitude of the EM field.

By dividing the output by the input we get our transmission spectrum.

